Muse Spark Open Kernel Challenge entries, team erkin98.

Four of the five kernels are derived from the public solutions in
https://github.com/vjeux/okc-2026 at commit f35a41ee1c13e316dabbf772830d47b23b453393
(Apache License, Version 2.0). Each file keeps that attribution in its header and marks
the lines we changed.

Ideas credited in the file headers:
- K-permutation of NVFP4 codes per stage: alygg77/okc-muse-spark-kernels
- 6-bit lossless NVFP4 block scales: keell0renz/muse-open-kernel-challenge
- Warp-parallel stream-K range computation: keell0renz/muse-open-kernel-challenge
- FP32 router input rule at up to 8 tokens: alygg77 and Matsvei

The prefill file reproduces the layer structure of SGLang (Apache License, Version 2.0)
at commit a55ab7d5ae1bba59ac351e55026fe7f7644ecc5f, as the organizers' task describes it.

Only ideas were taken from other teams' write-ups; no other team's code was copied.
